      "writtenOn": "2023-09-27T14:19:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nothing ever changes the current rounding mode, really :-) If you do, so many things break down. (The compiler also generally constant-folds expressions assuming the default mode, so you wouldn\u0027t even match that anymore.) And yes, the generated code improves with lrintf (especially now that we compile with -fno-math-errno). Whether it has an actual impact on a larger benchmark I cannot say for sure.\n\nAlso, of course, this trick (casting to higher precision) doesn\u0027t work if you want to round a double.",
